ressbook><name>TOMITA TOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAYAMA, KUNIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NGK INSULATORS, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMITA, TOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAYAMA KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMITA TOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAYAMA, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMITA, TOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A porous substrate which is made of a zeolite having the same composition as or a similar composition to that of a zeolite film to be formed thereon and contains a casting agent is coated with a zeolite containing the same casting agent. The coated substrate is calcined to remove the casting agent simultaneously from the zeolite coating and the porous substrate. Thus, a zeolite composite film is obtained which consists of the porous substrate and a zeolite film formed thereon. Since the zeolite film has been regulated so as to show almost the same thermal expansion behavior as the porous substrate, it does not develop cracks.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un substrat poreux en zéolithe qui présente la même composition ou une composition similaire à celle d'un film de zéolithe devant être formé sur celui-ci, et qui contient un agent de coulée, est revêtu d'une zéolithe contenant le même agent de coulée. Le substrat revêtu est calciné afin d'éliminer l'agent de coulée simultanément du revêtement de zéolithe et du substrat poreux. On obtient ainsi un film composite de zéolithe constitué du substrat poreux et d'un film de zéolithe formée sur celui-ci. Comme le film de zéolithe a été réglé de façon à présenter quasiment le même comportement d'expansion thermique que le substrat poreux, il ne produit pas de fissures.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>